DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("ln((x^4))");
$fun_1 = Formula("((ln((x^3))))^(1/2)");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("(({-10, -1, 3, 9} U {-10, -1, 3, 9}) U (4, 8)) U (4, 8) U ((4, 8) U (((4, 8)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (4, 8))))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("(4, 8) U {-10, -1, 3, 9}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-10, -1, 3, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (4, 8)) U ({-10, -1, 3, 9} U ({-10, -1, 3, 9}) U (4, 8))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("({-6, 6, 7} - ({-9, -5, 6, 7}))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-9, -5, 6, 7} U {-9, -5, 6, 7}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`10.59+9`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('19.59'),width=>2}
---

What is the value of [`3+1.07-19.72/17`]? [_____]{2.91}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-9, -5, 6, 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-6, 6, 7\}`]
- [`C = \{-10, -9, -8, -1, 0\}`]

Compute:
- [`B - (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -1, 3, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 4 < x < 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`((A \cup A) \cup B) \cup B \cup (B \cup ((B) \cap B)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cap B \cup (A \cup (A) \cup B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, 2, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, 2, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 4, 3, -6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 2, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, 2, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, 2, 3>") x Compute("<4, 3, -6>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<4, 3, -6>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, 3, -6>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<8, 2, 3>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, -2, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -1, -2, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -4, -10, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -2, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -2, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-6, -2, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, -10, 10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -2, 7>") x Compute("<-4, -10, 10>")}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -10, 10>") . Compute("<-1, -2, 10>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(9) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>9)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
